{"id": "EUVD-2026-108735", "enisaUuid": "9febb374-fc52-34f2-b5f0-b71a20f22c4c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nInput: ati_remote2 - fix type confusion in device attribute handlers\n\nPreviously, the channel_mask and mode_mask attributes were registered on\nthe parent usb_device via sysfs_create_group(). When commit b20d6bf8014b\n(\"Input: ati-remote2 - use driver core to instantiate device\nattributes\") converted the driver to let the driver core manage them via\ndev_groups in struct usb_driver, the attributes moved to the bound\nusb_interface devices, but the show and store callbacks were not updated\naccordingly.\n\nAs a result, the callbacks still invoked to_usb_device() on a device\npointer belonging to a struct usb_interface, producing an invalid\nusb_device pointer.\n\nUse to_usb_interface() directly in the attribute handlers to obtain the\ninterface and its driver data.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:23:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:23:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e44ec6b6d3c0b8ea089b589fa0cce49a4da66b89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d738e51bf2c21921df351f536147178ae3cbd38b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2caae9d1977beea0a7914b3d86639262801fd116", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f321cc430c49b6c1be0d53f2ef19d8342d8029cc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99069"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c52953c-d80e-37a7-b391-b9eebf6b9a91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "138504c4-7c6b-330e-9820-df3a6426d76e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "14170cfb-ead8-3bdb-90a2-219504f766f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "2e33a0b2-ba87-34fa-bff6-01d0643f752b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b20d6bf8014b2d6fcf65c150453d95a6276fd1fa <f321cc430c49b6c1be0d53f2ef19d8342d8029cc"}, {"id": "5491723b-1e9a-3444-9eaa-25af4775c0dd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "79de6e21-1318-3c2d-9af5-35910b91d969", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "86efc1e0-8f59-3860-89be-677df580e4aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b20d6bf8014b2d6fcf65c150453d95a6276fd1fa <d738e51bf2c21921df351f536147178ae3cbd38b"}, {"id": "921fc2b8-85f3-3e5e-97b4-e7f83d64e719", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b20d6bf8014b2d6fcf65c150453d95a6276fd1fa <2caae9d1977beea0a7914b3d86639262801fd116"}, {"id": "96300b4b-8ae9-3fb7-ba8d-a85b05c8cdfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b20d6bf8014b2d6fcf65c150453d95a6276fd1fa <e44ec6b6d3c0b8ea089b589fa0cce49a4da66b89"}, {"id": "c6978204-4119-3f46-8e9b-79b4c5dbf076", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b65d067-9f0f-3d53-ab05-766640063e92", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}